IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `je54-nouns`
IMPORT `je54-vintage`
IMPORT `je54-schedule-definitions`

-- je54-art02-05-words: Articles 2, 3 and 5 of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 (rules of words, "person" and bodies corporate, commonly used names), for a given TEXT of the Law.
-- Articles 4 and the Schedule are in je54-schedule-definitions; Article 3 is read with the Schedule definition of "person" (Article 4(1)).
-- Selecting date: the day the question is asked about (all seven deposited texts say the same in these Articles; before 1 January 2019 the module refuses).

§ `Article 2: Rules as to gender, number and grammatical variations of words defined`

-- src:13 | In this Law and in every other enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, unless the contrary intention appears –
-- src:14 | (a) words importing the masculine gender shall include females;
-- src:15 | (b) words in the singular shall include the plural and words in the plural shall include the singular; and
-- src:16 | (c) grammatical variations of words to which definitions are assigned shall be construed in accordance with the definitions.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 2 (src:13-16)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 2: a contrary intention appears, and the Article does not decide` MEANS
    REFUSE "a contrary intention appears: Article 2 does not say how the word is then read"

-- src:14 | (a) words importing the masculine gender shall include females;
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 2(a) (src:14)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 2(a) says nothing about words importing the feminine gender` MEANS
    REFUSE "Article 2(a) says that words importing the masculine gender include females; it says nothing about words importing the feminine gender"

-- src:13 | In this Law and in every other enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, unless the contrary intention appears –
-- src:14 | (a) words importing the masculine gender shall include females;
-- src:15 | (b) words in the singular shall include the plural and words in the plural shall include the singular; and
-- src:16 | (c) grammatical variations of words to which definitions are assigned shall be construed in accordance with the definitions.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 2 (src:13-16)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of word under Article 2`
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Reach of a word under Article 2`
`the reach of a word under Article 2` kind `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `a contrary intention appears` THEN `Article 2: a contrary intention appears, and the Article does not decide`
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER kind
               WHEN `a word importing the masculine gender` THEN `the word includes females`
               WHEN `a word importing the feminine gender` THEN `Article 2(a) says nothing about words importing the feminine gender`
               WHEN `a word in the singular` THEN `the word includes the plural`
               WHEN `a word in the plural` THEN `the word includes the singular`
               WHEN `a grammatical variation of a word to which a definition is assigned` THEN `the word is construed in accordance with the definition`

-- src:13 | In this Law and in every other enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, unless the contrary intention appears –
-- src:14 | (a) words importing the masculine gender shall include females;
-- src:15 | (b) words in the singular shall include the plural and words in the plural shall include the singular; and
-- src:16 | (c) grammatical variations of words to which definitions are assigned shall be construed in accordance with the definitions.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 2 (src:13-16)
GIVEN v IS A `Text of the Law`
      kind IS A `Kind of word under Article 2`
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Reach of a word under Article 2`
`Article 2: how a word is read` v kind `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the text of the Law is one of the seven deposited texts` v THEN `the Law has no deposited text for a day before the first consolidated version`
           OTHERWISE `the reach of a word under Article 2` kind `a contrary intention appears`

§ `Article 3: Application of penal enactments to bodies corporate`

-- src:18 | In the construction of every enactment relating to a punishable offence, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, the expression “person” shall, unless the contrary intention appears, include a body corporate:
-- src:19 | Provided that nothing in this Article shall render any body corporate liable, in respect of any act or omission occurring before the date of the commencement of this Law, to any criminal proceedings to which that body corporate would not have been liable before that date.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 3 (src:18-19)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 3: a contrary intention appears, and the Article does not decide` MEANS
    REFUSE "a contrary intention appears: Article 3 does not say whether person then includes a body corporate"

-- src:18 | In the construction of every enactment relating to a punishable offence, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, the expression “person” shall, unless the contrary intention appears, include a body corporate:
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 3 (src:18)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 3 deals only with an enactment relating to a punishable offence` MEANS
    REFUSE "Article 3 deals only with an enactment relating to a punishable offence; for any other enactment see the Schedule definition of person"

-- The proviso: "nothing in this Article shall render any body corporate liable, in respect of any act or omission occurring before the date of the commencement of this Law, to any criminal proceedings to which that
-- body corporate would not have been liable before that date".  The date of the commencement of the Law is 21 August 1954 (Table of Legislation History).  An act on 21 August 1954 itself is not before that date.
-- src:19 | Provided that nothing in this Article shall render any body corporate liable, in respect of any act or omission occurring before the date of the commencement of this Law, to any criminal proceedings to which that body corporate would not have been liable before that date.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 3, proviso (src:19)
GIVEN `the day of the act or omission` IS A DATE
      `the body corporate would have been liable to the proceedings before that date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the proviso to Article 3 withholds liability` `the day of the act or omission` `the body corporate would have been liable to the proceedings before that date` MEANS
        `the day of the act or omission` LESS THAN `the day on which the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 came into force`
    AND NOT `the body corporate would have been liable to the proceedings before that date`

-- src:18 | In the construction of every enactment relating to a punishable offence, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, the expression “person” shall, unless the contrary intention appears, include a body corporate:
-- src:19 | Provided that nothing in this Article shall render any body corporate liable, in respect of any act or omission occurring before the date of the commencement of this Law, to any criminal proceedings to which that body corporate would not have been liable before that date.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 3 (src:18-19)
GIVEN v IS A `Text of the Law`
      `the enactment relates to a punishable offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the act or omission` IS A DATE
      `the body corporate would have been liable to the proceedings before that date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 3: person includes a body corporate` v `the enactment relates to a punishable offence` `a contrary intention appears` `the day of the act or omission` `the body corporate would have been liable to the proceedings before that date` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the text of the Law is one of the seven deposited texts` v THEN `the Law has no deposited text for a day before the first consolidated version`
           IF NOT `the enactment relates to a punishable offence` THEN `Article 3 deals only with an enactment relating to a punishable offence`
           IF `a contrary intention appears` THEN `Article 3: a contrary intention appears, and the Article does not decide`
           OTHERWISE NOT `the proviso to Article 3 withholds liability` `the day of the act or omission` `the body corporate would have been liable to the proceedings before that date`

-- Article 3 with the Schedule definition of "person" (Article 4(1)).  Fork I5: the proviso says "nothing in this Article", so on the reading taken it limits Article 3 and not the Schedule's definition (inserted by
-- L.16/2003, applying to every enactment whenever passed or made); on the other reading the proviso also limits the Schedule definition for a body corporate.  A body of persons unincorporated is never within Article 3
-- (which says body corporate) and never within the proviso.
-- src:18 | In the construction of every enactment relating to a punishable offence, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, the expression “person” shall, unless the contrary intention appears, include a body corporate:
-- src:19 | Provided that nothing in this Article shall render any body corporate liable, in respect of any act or omission occurring before the date of the commencement of this Law, to any criminal proceedings to which that body corporate would not have been liable before that date.
-- src:105 | “month” shall mean a calendar month;
-- src:106 | “oath” shall, in the case of a person for the time being allowed by law to affirm or declare instead of swearing, include affirmation and declaration;
-- src:107 | “parent”, in relation to a child, includes a person who is that child’s parent by virtue of Schedule A1 to the Children (Jersey) Law 2002;
-- src:108 | “person” shall include any body of persons corporate or unincorporated;
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 3 (src:18-19); Schedule, Part 1, definition of “person” (src:108)
GIVEN v IS A `Text of the Law`
      kind IS A `Kind of body`
      `the enactment relates to a punishable offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the act or omission` IS A DATE
      `the body corporate would have been liable to the proceedings before that date` IS A BOOLEAN
      reading IS A `Reach of the proviso to Article 3` TYPICALLY `the proviso limits Article 3 only`
GIVETH A `How person reaches a body`
`how person reaches the body` v kind `the enactment relates to a punishable offence` `a contrary intention appears` `the day of the act or omission` `the body corporate would have been liable to the proceedings before that date` reading MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the text of the Law is one of the seven deposited texts` v THEN `the Law has no deposited text for a day before the first consolidated version`
           IF `a contrary intention appears` THEN `Article 3: a contrary intention appears, and the Article does not decide`
           OTHERWISE
               LET byArticle3 MEANS
                       kind EQUALS `a body corporate`
                   AND `the enactment relates to a punishable offence`
                   AND NOT `the proviso to Article 3 withholds liability` `the day of the act or omission` `the body corporate would have been liable to the proceedings before that date`
               IN LET bySchedule MEANS
                          kind EQUALS `a body of persons that is unincorporated`
                       OR CONSIDER reading
                          WHEN `the proviso limits Article 3 only` THEN TRUE
                          WHEN `the proviso also limits the Schedule definition of person` THEN
                              NOT `the proviso to Article 3 withholds liability` `the day of the act or omission` `the body corporate would have been liable to the proceedings before that date`
                  IN BRANCH IF byArticle3 AND bySchedule THEN `by Article 3 and by the Schedule`
                            IF byArticle3 THEN `by Article 3 only`
                            IF bySchedule THEN `by the Schedule only`
                            OTHERWISE `not at all`

§ `Article 5: Commonly used names`

-- src:24 | In an enactment, unless the context otherwise requires, the name commonly applied to a country, place, body, administration, corporation, society, officer, functionary, person, party or thing shall mean the country, place, body, administration, corporation, society, officer, functionary, person, party or thing to which the name is commonly applied, whether or not the name is the formal or unabbreviated designation thereof.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 5 (src:24)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 5: the context requires otherwise, and the Article does not decide` MEANS
    REFUSE "the context otherwise requires: Article 5 does not say what the name then means"

-- The name commonly applied to a country, place, body, administration, corporation, society, officer, functionary, person, party or thing shall mean the thing to which the name is commonly applied, whether or not the
-- name is the formal or unabbreviated designation.  The list ends in "thing", so every kind of thing is covered and no kind is an input.  The thing to which the name is commonly applied is the caller's fact.
-- src:24 | In an enactment, unless the context otherwise requires, the name commonly applied to a country, place, body, administration, corporation, society, officer, functionary, person, party or thing shall mean the country, place, body, administration, corporation, society, officer, functionary, person, party or thing to which the name is commonly applied, whether or not the name is the formal or unabbreviated designation thereof.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 5 (src:24)
GIVEN v IS A `Text of the Law`
      `the thing to which the name is commonly applied` IS A STRING
      `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A STRING
`Article 5: what a commonly used name means` v `the thing to which the name is commonly applied` `the context otherwise requires` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the text of the Law is one of the seven deposited texts` v THEN `the Law has no deposited text for a day before the first consolidated version`
           IF `the context otherwise requires` THEN `Article 5: the context requires otherwise, and the Article does not decide`
           OTHERWISE `the thing to which the name is commonly applied`
